    {
      "name": "RM554484",
      "value_name": "RM554484",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding boolean:\nCustomer could hear some glitch noise when P-state change.\nThis is because we spend too much time on DPC_LEVEL.\nEnable this registry key can make p-state change at PASSIVE_LEVEL.\n0 (default) - P-state change will run at PASSIVE_LEVEL.\n1 - P-state change will run at DPC_LEVEL.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RM554484",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "LOW" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "HIGH" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM572548",
      "value_name": "RM572548",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding boolean:\nTo decide whether we need to busy-wait for sequencer after writing new sor power settings.\nzero (default) - Wait blockingly for sequencer operation to finish.\nnonzero - Do not wait.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RM572548",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM580312",
      "value_name": "RM580312",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "This key is an override for the OPSB feature (more information below). The\nRM_OPSB key will not be given to customers, this is being added as a way\nto provide a safer key that can override the feature as a whole.\nBug 580312.\nType Binary\nLength:\nNumber of Bytes to read.\nEncoding:\nENABLE    enables the feature\nDISABLE   disables the feature",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RM580312",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "LENGTH" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM592311",
      "value_name": "RM592311",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nOriginally this option was in RMOPSB, but we have decided to give it\nits own regkey. This controls whether or not we allow a mclk switching\nin dual head.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "ENABLE",
          "bits": [0, 1],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "TRUE" },
            { "value": 2, "name": "FALSE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM624000",
      "value_name": "RM624000",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding boolean:\nTo decide whether RM need to busy-wait for NV_PGRAPH_STATUS_FE_METHOD_LOWER_IDLE for Bug 624000\n1  Wait for NV_PGRAPH_STATUS_FE_METHOD_LOWER_IDLE for Bug 624000\nzero(default) - Do not wait, No WAR\nthis reg key is only for full chip RTL runs, on silicon after injecting the bundle RM busy waits for\nstatus NV_PGRAPH_STATUS_FE_METHOD_LOWER_IDLE because of Bug 624000 , on RTL runs if its enaled by default\nit can cause perf slowdown issues, its temporary regkey will get removed in future chips after GK20x",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RM624000",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "WAIT_FOR_LOWER_IDLE_NO" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "WAIT_FOR_LOWER_IDLE_YES" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM625316",
      "value_name": "RM625316",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding boolean\nzero (default) -- Keep the prefetch enabled\nnonzero        -- Disable the prefetch from CROP/ZROP to SYS/PEER/VIDMEM.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RM625316",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM628700",
      "value_name": "RM628700",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding boolean.\nThis'll tell us whether Optimus system is treated as headless?\nBased on this Do / Skip the display output device detection as a part of WAR [for bug 628700]\nas there was a false load detect on some of the Optimus systems due to HW design issue.\n0 - System is not headless\n!0 - System is headless",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RM628700",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "NOTHEADLESS" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "HEADLESS" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM64KBBAR1Mappings",
      "value_name": "RM64KBBAR1Mappings",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Disable 64KB BAR1 mappings\n0 - Disable 64KB BAR1 mappings\n1 - Force/Enable 64KB BAR1 mappings",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RM64KBBAR1Mappings",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DISABLED" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLED" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM654663",
      "value_name": "RM654663",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding NvU32\nNumber of iterations to see an interrupt in succession before considering it\nstuck.\nDefault - See INTR_STUCK_THRESHOLD"
    },
    {
      "name": "Rm719476",
      "value_name": "Rm719476",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "TYPE DWORD\nThis registry key is activated only when a GSYNC HULK license is present.\nIt allows the driver to bypass the NVSR panel PACD EDID check.\nDefault is NV_REG_STR_RM_NVSR_BYPASS_NVSR_PACD_CHECK_NO: do not bypass",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "Rm719476",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "NO" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "YES" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM776993",
      "value_name": "RM776993",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD:\nTreat DisplayPort Dual-Mode adaptor as DP2DVI (type 1) or DP2HDMI (type 2) dongle.\nBit  0:0  - Force all dongles as type 1 (165 MHz TMDS clock rate).\nBit  1:1  - Force all dongles as type 2 (300 MHz TMDS clock rate).\nBit  7:2  - Reserved.\nBit 15:8  - The linkMask of target links. The dongles on specified links are\ntreated as type 1 or type 2 forcedly and it depends on bit 0 or 1 is set.\nBit 31:16 - Reserved.\nEncoding Bitmask: There are two types of linkMask.\nFor Pre-GM20X (with non-split SOR VBIOS), the linkMask is considered as sorSublinkMask here.\nBit  9:8  - SOR 0 (sublink A & B)\nBit 11:10 - SOR 1 (sublink A & B)\nBit 13:12 - SOR 2 (sublink A & B)\nBit 15:14 - SOR 3 (sublink A & B)\nFor GM20x+, the linkMask is considered as padLinkMask here.\nBit  9:8  - Pad Macro 0 (macro sublink 0 & 1)\nBit 11:10 - Pad Macro 1 (macro sublink 0 & 1)\nBit 13:12 - Pad Macro 2 (macro sublink 0 & 1)\nBit 15:14 - Pad Macro 3 (macro sublink 0 & 1)",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "TYPE_1",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "TRUE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "TYPE_2",
          "bits": [1],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "TRUE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "LINK_MASK",
          "bits": [8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM839040",
      "value_name": "RM839040",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding boolean\nOverride to disable storing bad FB memory pages or row-remappings to InfoROM.\nzero (default) -- Disable Dynamic DRAM retirement.\nnonzero        -- Enable Dynamic DRAM retirement.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RM839040",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RM922492",
      "value_name": "RM922492",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "TYPE DWORD\nEncoding:  If non-zero, then the DockWar922492 event is used instead of\nInduceDeviceScan for undocked->dock transitions."
    },
    {
      "name": "RM976975",
      "value_name": "RM976975",
      "key_paths": [
