      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding boolean.\nAvoid frequently reading GPU timer by tmrDelay when GPU busy or unstable.\nDevelopers should take care of this flag, using one of osDelay functions instead of tmrDelay,\nwhen they have trouble with tmrDelay when GPU busy/unstable.\n0 - Follow old behavior\n1 - Use osDelay functions when possible with GPU busy/unstable cases\nDefault 0",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RMAvoidBusyReadingTimer",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RMBandwidthFeature",
      "value_name": "RMBandwidthFeature",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Scaler amortization reduces hubclk and dispclk requirements by allowing the\nfetch of the scaler's input line to be spread across an entire raster line\ntime.  The feature is not supported (and should not be enabled) on chips\nprior to Orin.\nNote that if the reg key is used to disable scaler amortization, it will\nprevent RM from forcing the scaler to be enabled for non-scaled configs, and\nit will cause IMP to use legacy calculations for hubclk and dispclk, but it\nwill not actually disable HW amortization on 2-TAP scaled configs.\nNote: If precharge powerdown is enabled instead of ASR (which is expected on\nGM20X and later; see PDB_PROP_FB_USE_PRECHARGE_POWERDOWN_INSTEAD_OF_ASR_DEF),\nthen the ASR feature control will control precharge powerdown.\nFORCE_MIN_MEMPOOL must be disabled if DYNAMIC_MEMPOOL is disabled.\nWhen enabling experimental IMP support during early chip bringup, you may\nalso need to enable various related bandwidth feature flags such as STUTTER,\nDYNAMIC_MEMPOOL, LINE_BUFFERING, and MEMPOOL_COMPRESSION and disable others,\nsuch as FORCE_MIN_MEMPOOL.  When in doubt, ask an RM engineer.\nReserved in case we want to extend _FEATURES_IMP to include more properties.\nThe line buffering control is initially implemented for GF10X only.\nNote: Line buffering cannot be disabled on NvDisplay (this reg key will be\nignored).\nThis control limits mempool allocation to the minimum number of blocks\nnecessary to support latency and avoid underflow.  Line buffering and\nASR/MSCG will be disabled, because those features require more than the\nminimum allocation.  Note also that some modes may become not possible\nas a result of line buffering being disabled, due to the increased bandwidth\nrequirement.\nDYNAMIC_MEMPOOL must be enabled if FORCE_MIN_MEMPOOL is enabled.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "DEPRECATED_0",
          "bits": [0, 1]
        },
        {
          "name": "ISO_CRIT_ALWAYS",
          "bits": [2, 3],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "SCALER_AMORTIZATION",
          "bits": [4, 5],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "DEPRECATED_2",
          "bits": [6, 7]
        },
        {
          "name": "DEPRECATED_3",
          "bits": [8, 9]
        },
        {
          "name": "ASR",
          "bits": [10, 11],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "DEPRECATED_4",
          "bits": [12, 13]
        },
        {
          "name": "DYNAMIC_MEMPOOL",
          "bits": [14, 15],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "DEPRECATED_5",
          "bits": [16, 17]
        },
        {
          "name": "IMP",
          "bits": [18, 19],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "RESERVED",
          "bits": [20, 21]
        },
        {
          "name": "DEPRECATED_6",
          "bits": [22, 23]
        },
        {
          "name": "DYNAMIC_DISP_CLK",
          "bits": [24, 25],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "DEPRECATED_7",
          "bits": [26, 27]
        },
        {
          "name": "LINE_BUFFERING",
          "bits": [28, 29],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "FORCE_MIN_MEMPOOL",
          "bits": [30, 31],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RMBandwidthFeature2",
      "value_name": "RMBandwidthFeature2",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "With advanced and old fetch metering supported in HW, this regkey helps\noverriding the current mechanism with the other one.\nENABLE:  Advanced fetch metering is enabled and will override if old fetch\nfetch metering is enabled in HW by default.\nDISABLE: Advanced fetch metering is disabled if it is already enabled by\ndefault in HW.\nNote: Currently in Ampere and later chips advanced fetch metering is enabled\nby default in HW and it may change in Orin.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "MEMPOOL_COMPRESSION",
          "bits": [0, 1],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "ADVANCED_FETCH_METERING",
          "bits": [2, 3],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RMBar1ApertureSizeMB",
      "value_name": "RMBar1ApertureSizeMB",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding Numeric Value\nOverrides the size of the BAR1 aperture. Used to shrink BAR1. It cannot be\ngreater than the physical size of BAR1."
    },
    {
      "name": "RMBar1RestoreSize",
      "value_name": "RMBar1RestoreSize",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD:\nEncoding -- Boolean\nCheck if BAR1 size has been restored correctly by SBIOS across power transitions\nDefault: enabled for Ampere and up"
    },
    {
      "name": "RMBar2ApertureSizeMB",
      "value_name": "RMBar2ApertureSizeMB",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding Numeric Value\nOverrides the size of the BAR2 aperture.  Cannot be greater than the\nphysical size of BAR2 available to RM (which may be less than the total size\nof BAR2).  When this regkey is present we cap the total aperture size to the\nRM aperture size. This can result in undefined beahvior in environments that\nrely on a virtual bar2 aperture shared between RM and VBIOS for VESA support."
    },
    {
      "name": "RMBar2BaseGB",
      "value_name": "RMBar2BaseGB",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding Numeric Value\nOverrides the base VA of BAR2. Cannot be greater than\n(Max supported VA limit) - (BAR2 cpu invisible aperture size) as we would overflow the max VA Limit\nWhen this regkey is present the BAR2 VA mappings will be in the range of\nNV_REG_STR_RM_BAR2_BASE : BAR2 aperture size"
    },
    {
      "name": "RMBar2SysmemEnable",
      "value_name": "RMBar2SysmemEnable",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Allows BAR2 to use the GPU's mmu for sysmem surfaces instead of directly accessing sysmem using\ncpu pointers. Available only on verif environments\nType DWORD\nEncoding: see below\nSYSMEM_ENABLE_FALSE: (Default) BAR2 sysmem surfaces will use direct cpu mapping of sysmem\nSYSMEM_ENABLE_TRUE : BAR2 sysmem surfaces will use bar2 page tables\nAllow instance memory overrides.  Some fields are chip specific\nand may not apply to all chips.  Since there are many fields,\nthis is spread across several DWORD registry keys.\nThe registry keys are defined in nvrm_registry.\nSpecific overrrides are defined here.\nEncoding:\nDEFAULT   RM determines\nCOH       Coherent system memory\nNCOH      Non-coherent system memory\nVID       Local video memory\nSeparately define instance block location of BARs. Default Setting\nreverts to NV_REG_STR_RM_INST_LOC_INSTBLK\nSeparately define instance block location of async CEs. Default Setting\nSeparately define instance block location of GR/GRCE. Default Setting\nSeparately define instance block location of VEs. Default Setting\nSeparately define instance block location of HWPM PMA. Default Setting",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "ENABLE",
          "bits": [0, 1],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "TRUE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RmBlackListAddresses",
      "value_name": "RmBlackListAddresses",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type BINARY:\nstruct\n{\nNvU64 addresses[NV2080_CTRL_FB_OFFLINED_PAGES_MAX_PAGES];\n};"
    },
    {
      "name": "RMBlcg",
      "value_name": "RMBlcg",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nThis regKey is used for Block Level Clock Gating settings\nEach engine uses 4 bits. For this regkey to be used, RmPowerFeatures\ncorresponding to this feature(21:18) should have a value of 2\nThe bottom 2 bits, decide if the feature is off/on/default for the engine\nThe top two bits decide the level of BLCG (stall, idle or quiescent), if\nBLCG has been enabled/default for the engine\n0 : Keep the vbios default\n1 : Disable feature\n3 : Enable feature\n4 : IDLE\n8 : STALL\nC : QUIESCENT\nNOTE: FOllowing engines share same regkey\nFB, FBPA, LTCG and XBAR share bit 11:8\nAll other engines not mentioned below share bit 31:28\nEach engine uses 4 bits:\n- Bottom 2 bits: off/on/default\n- Top 2 bits: level (idle, stall, quiescent)",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "GR",
          "bits": [0, 1, 2, 3],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" },
            { "value": 7, "name": "IDLE" },
            { "value": 11, "name": "STALL" },
            { "value": 15, "name": "QUIESCENT" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "PPP",
          "bits": [4, 5, 6, 7],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" },
            { "value": 7, "name": "IDLE" },
            { "value": 11, "name": "STALL" },
            { "value": 15, "name": "QUIESCENT" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "FB",
          "bits": [8, 9, 10, 11],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" },
            { "value": 7, "name": "IDLE" },
            { "value": 11, "name": "STALL" },
            { "value": 15, "name": "QUIESCENT" }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "PDEC",
          "bits": [12, 13, 14, 15],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "ENABLE" },
