    {
      "name": "RMGlitchlessModeset",
      "value_name": "RMGlitchlessModeset",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\n0 - Default (same as if the reg key had not been used).\n1 - Performs a glitchless transition on all modesets where it is possible,\nregardless of what the client requested.\n2 - Performs a glitchless transition on all modesets where (1) glitchless\ntransition is possible, and (2) the client has requested a glitchless\ntransition.\n3 - Does not perform modesets glitchlessly even if requested by the client;\nCAP reports to the client that the feature is not available.\n4 - Does not perform modesets glitchlessly even if requested by the client,\nbut the CAP reports to the client that the feature is available (for\ndebug only).\nNote: The above policies refer to extended cases of possible glitchless\nmodesets, such as when scaling factors change, as requested in bug 1810907.\nCertain basic transition cases, such as enabling and disabling an overlay,\nwill be glitchless, regardless of this policy setting.\nReg key added for Mods requirement.\nMods can override the perf limits, to include CLIENT_LOW* limits in the IMP query\nex: When reg key is supplied with NV2080_CTRL_PERF_PERF_LIMIT_ID_ISMODEPOSSIBLE(0x47) the\ndefault value will be set. Value of NV2080_CTRL_PERF_PERF_LIMIT_ID* can be found in\nctrl2080perf.h\nMods argument: -imp_perf_limit_mask 0x47",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RMGlitchlessModeset",
          "bits": [0, 1, 2],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ALL_MODESETS" },
            { "value": 2, "name": "CLIENT_CONTROL" },
            { "value": 3, "name": "LEGACY" },
            { "value": 4, "name": "LEGACY_BUT_REPORT_FEATURE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RmGlobalPoisonOverride",
      "value_name": "RmGlobalPoisonOverride",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Override the HW fuse - Global Poison Enable, for internal SKU GA100\nwhich are post ECO. Post ECO GA100 use SM_TTU fuse for Global poison fuse and\nas per Bug 2857928, VBIOS will enable Global poison using feature override register\n(NV_FUSE_FEATURE_OVERRIDE_QUADRO {_SM_TTU_OVERRIDE | _SM_TTU} )for post ECO\nGA100 internal SKU's (both signed and unsigned INT-* and V0*) and also remove\nPLM protection for NV_FUSE_FEATURE_OVERRIDE_QUADRO register on internal SKUs.\nThis will enable RM to disable Global poison fuse for MODS builds.\nThe registry key allows users (MODS, QA) to enable or disable the Global Poison\nfuse on internal SKU's of post ECO GA100 GPU.\nType: DWORD\n_DEFAULT - This value will not override and will instead use the HW fuse\n_ENABLE  - This value will enable Global Poison HW fuse\n_DISABLE - This value will disable Global Poison HW fuse",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RmGlobalPoisonOverride",
          "bits": [0, 1],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLE" },
            { "value": 2, "name": "DISABLE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RMGpcTileMap",
      "value_name": "RMGpcTileMap",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type String\nencoded string to setup the GPC/TPC screen tile mapping\nthe encoding is V0:V2:V3:VN\nwhere V? is the table entry represented  by a valid GPC number\nnumber of entries must equal the # TPC in the system\nentry numbers must be 0..N, where N is (#GPC's - 1)"
    },
    {
      "name": "RMGpioPmuMutexTimeoutus",
      "value_name": "RMGpioPmuMutexTimeoutus",
      "key_paths": [
