      ],
      "bit_width": 32
    },
    {
      "name": "RmGpsUtilHystHighBatt",
      "value_name": "RmGpsUtilHystHighBatt",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD (signed)"
    },
    {
      "name": "RmGpsUtilHystHighBBoost",
      "value_name": "RmGpsUtilHystHighBBoost",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD (signed)"
    },
    {
      "name": "RmGpsUtilHystLow",
      "value_name": "RmGpsUtilHystLow",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nType DWORD (signed)\nThis two registry keys (RmGpsUtilHystHigh & RmGpsUtilHystLow) define a\nwindow [(gpuUtil-utilHystLow)..(gpuUtil-utilHystHigh)] in which GPS will\nattempt to maintain CPU utilization.\nBoth high and low deltas are in the range [-100% .. 100%] and\n(RmGpsUtilHystHigh < RmGpsUtilHystLow)\nThese are the global overrides, below are the values specific to AC,\nbattery, and BatteryBoost modes."
    },
    {
      "name": "RmGpsUtilHystLowAc",
      "value_name": "RmGpsUtilHystLowAc",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD (signed)"
    },
    {
      "name": "RmGpsUtilHystLowBatt",
      "value_name": "RmGpsUtilHystLowBatt",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD (signed)"
    },
    {
      "name": "RmGpsUtilHystLowBBoost",
      "value_name": "RmGpsUtilHystLowBBoost",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD (signed)\nThese allow the windows for AC, battery, and BatteryBoost modes to be\ndefined separately, and will override the values set by RmGpuUtilHystHigh\nand RmGpuUtilHystLow for those modes."
    },
    {
      "name": "RmGpsWebPoll",
      "value_name": "RmGpsWebPoll",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nSet the polling interval (in ms) for the WEB controller\nExplanation on NV_REG_STR_RM_GPS_WEB_POLL_DEFAULT: if we want to set the WEB\npolling interval to a default value, just use NV_REG_STR_RM_GPS_WEB_POLL_DEFAULT.\nAlthough it is defined to be 0, the default polling interval is\nSPB_GPS_WEB_DEFAULT_POLLING_INTVL, which is defined in objspbgps.c",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RmGpsWebPoll",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
