        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding boolean\nDefault FALSE",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RMZBCFlushEnable",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DEFAULT" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "TRUE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RMZcullEqualScreenDistOnFS",
      "value_name": "RMZcullEqualScreenDistOnFS",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "TYPE Dword\nRegkey based solution to enable Zcull equal screen distribution among GPCs.\nThe feature is disable by default and could be enabled through the\nfollowing regkey.\n1 - Enable zcull equal screen distribution",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RMZcullEqualScreenDistOnFS",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "FALSE" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "TRUE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "romOverride\\0\\0\\0",
      "value_name": "romOverride\\0\\0\\0",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type Binary\nReasoning: This regkey is solely to be used when changing the BIOS or driver binary\nis not allowed.  If BIOS is allowed to change, the real fix should go there.\nIf BIOS must remain the same, but the driver is allowed to change, then\nwe should move the regkey into the driver and remove it from the INF.\nName Mangling: Note, the first ROM Override will be listed as romOverride00. The 10th\nROM Override will be listed as romOverride0A.  The 16th ROM Override will\nbe listed as romOverride10.  Max ROM Override will be romOverrideFF (256).\nEncoding:\nBytes 0-3: BIOS Number: Example: 4.17.00.22.13 would be listed as\n0x04 0x17 0x00 0x22\nByte  4:   BIOS OEM Number: For production BIOSes, these numbers will\nbe used to single out one BIOS sku. Example: 4.17.00.22.13 would be\nlisted as 0x13.  If this value in the registry is 0x00, then all bioses\nthat match the main BIOS number will be overridden.\nBytes 5-8: 32 bit offset (Byte 5 - Least significant byte) that defines the starting\nbyte in the image to override.\nByte  9:   Number of bytes in this override.  Max: 246 bytes for each override.  This\nlists the number of bytes starting with byte 10 to the end of the regkey.\nBytes 10+  Individual bytes that will be overridden in the bios.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "romOverride\\0\\0\\0",
          "bits": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8],
          "states": [
            { "value": 256, "name": "MAX_REG_ROM_OVERRIDES", "meaning": "Type Binary" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "RunOnlyNVSR",
      "value_name": "RunOnlyNVSR",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nThis regkey controls if there should be only SR step in the sequence\nof NVSR GC6 flavors\nThis is for HW testing only",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "RunOnlyNVSR",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DISABLED" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLED" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "SBIOSHandlesHotkeyInhibit",
      "value_name": "SBIOSHandlesHotkeyInhibit",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding Bitmask\nBit 1 -- SBIOS can be trusted to inhibit hotkeys correctly",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "B1",
          "bits": [1],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "FALSE", "meaning": "Default or unspecified behavior" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "TRUE", "meaning": "SBIOS can be trusted to inhibit hotkeys" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "SkipSwStateErrChecks",
      "value_name": "SkipSwStateErrChecks",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nWhen set to a non-zero value tells RM to skip the state err checks supplied\nby arch team. Default is 0 which means state err checks won't be skipped."
    },
    {
      "name": "SlideMCLK",
      "value_name": "SlideMCLK",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding 1 = Enable, 0 = Disable\nWhen enabled, this gradually slides MCLK top its new value.  This works around\nPLL settle time and DLL reset issues.  Only works with two-stage PLLs.\nDefault is enabled.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "SlideMCLK",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "SmoothBrightnessDefaultEnable",
      "value_name": "SmoothBrightnessDefaultEnable",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type REG_DWORD\nSpecifies the default state of the smooth brightness\nfeature"
    },
    {
      "name": "SmoothBrightnessStepIntervalMs",
      "value_name": "SmoothBrightnessStepIntervalMs",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type REG_DWORD\nSpecifies the number of milliseconds between smooth brightness\nupdates"
    },
    {
      "name": "SmoothBrightnessTransitionTimeDownMs",
      "value_name": "SmoothBrightnessTransitionTimeDownMs",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type REG_DWORD\nSpecifies the number of milliseconds that a smooth brightness\ntransition that decreases the brightness will take"
    },
    {
      "name": "SmoothBrightnessTransitionTimeUpMs",
      "value_name": "SmoothBrightnessTransitionTimeUpMs",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type REG_DWORD\nSpecifies the number of milliseconds that a smooth brightness\ntransition that increases the brightness will take"
    },
    {
      "name": "SuppressClassList",
      "value_name": "SuppressClassList",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type String\nA list of comma separated classes to suppress\nexamples:\n5097\n4097, 5097\netc"
    },
    {
      "name": "syncRgDivs",
      "value_name": "syncRgDivs",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nA non-zero value will make RM try to use the same RG div on both heads\nwhen determining the VPLL values and accompanying dividers to program\nDoes not apply to Pascal and up"
    },
    {
      "name": "TestAnalogLoadAlways",
      "value_name": "TestAnalogLoadAlways",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding: !0 or N/A -- Default - When an EDIDs is found when detecting CRT or FP devices,\nalways run an analog load test to make sure that the device is or isn't\nan analog device. This registry key will affect all EDID reads. It\nattempts to fix bug 62052, 60478 on a grand scale.  But if set, it will\nunfix bug 55014, which will cause flashing on a flat panel when running\nanalog load detects for a CRT. NOTE: Now the default since we no longer\nsupport prior to NV4x and we've encountered issues with the below option.\n0 -- When finding an EDID that says it's digital when looking for an analog\ndevice, we'll not do any analog load test. NOTE: This is no longer the\ndefault! Various monitors/KVMs encounter trouble with this, but it's\nalso necessary for other monitors/KVMs. This is a no-win option.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "TestAnalogLoadAlways",
          "bits": [0],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLE" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "ThermalChipType",
      "value_name": "ThermalChipType",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Thermal chip type override\nType Dword\nEncoding Numeric Value\nValue can be used to disable or override thermal chip type in DCB\nRefer to dacdcb.h for supported values.\n0               -> thermal chip disabled (NV_MISCDCB_THERMALDIODE_SUPPORT_NA)\n// != 0xFFFFFFFF -> other thermal chip type (e.g. NV_MISCDCB_THERMALDIODE_SUPPORT_LM99)\nxFFFFFFFF       -> Default case. Normal DCB described operation"
    },
    {
      "name": "ThermalPolicySW1",
      "value_name": "ThermalPolicySW1",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type Dword\nEncoding bitmask\nBit     0: If == 0, disable thermal SW1 support\nBits 31-1: Reserved"
    },
    {
      "name": "ThermalSBH1",
      "value_name": "ThermalSBH1",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type Dword\nEncoding Numeric Value\nHysteresis value for SBIOS controlled Thermals for the T1 limit."
    },
    {
      "name": "ThermalSBH2",
      "value_name": "ThermalSBH2",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type Dword\nEncoding Numeric Value\nHysteresis value for SBIOS controlled Thermals for the T2 limit."
    },
    {
      "name": "ThermalThresh00Target000",
      "value_name": "ThermalThresh00Target000",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type Dword\nEncoding Numeric Value\nSet of values, where 00 is replaced by the threshold (so far, T1 = 01,\nT2 = 02) and 000 is replaced by the index into the Dell specific sensor\narray in SBMAX6649 (which is BIOS and device dependent). The numerical\nvalues are in decimal."
    },
    {
      "name": "TSwapRdyHiLsrMinTime",
      "value_name": "TSwapRdyHiLsrMinTime",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type: DWORD\nEncoding:\nTo modify LSR_MIN_TIME parameter according to the time\nperiod for which swap lock window will remain HIGH for QSYNC III\ni.e. P2060 during swap barrier.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "TSwapRdyHiLsrMinTime",
          "bits": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7],
          "states": [
            { "value": 250, "name": "DEFAULT", "meaning": "250 micro seconds" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "TSwapRdyHiSwapLockoutStart",
      "value_name": "TSwapRdyHiSwapLockoutStart",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type: DWORD\nEncoding:\nTo modify SWAP_LOCKOUT_START parameter according to the time\nperiod for which swap lock window will remain HIGH for QSYNC III.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "TSwapRdyHiSwapLockoutStart",
          "bits": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7],
          "states": [
            { "value": 250, "name": "DEFAULT", "meaning": "250 micro seconds" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "TwinViewDisabled",
      "value_name": "TwinViewDisabled",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncoding Numeric Value\nForce Single Head ?"
    },
    {
      "name": "UnlicensedRestricted1StateTimeout",
      "value_name": "UnlicensedRestricted1StateTimeout",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nContains the Restricted 1(Grid Unlicensed) state timeout value in mins."
    },
    {
      "name": "UnlicensedUnrestrictedStateTimeout",
      "value_name": "UnlicensedUnrestrictedStateTimeout",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nContains the Unrestricted(Grid Unlicensed) state timeout value in mins"
    },
    {
      "name": "UseGenericEDIDManufacturer",
      "value_name": "UseGenericEDIDManufacturer",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "The next registry keys are Toshiba-scecific, and are used to determine overdrive support on\ntheir LVDS panels."
    },
    {
      "name": "UseUncachedPCIMappings",
      "value_name": "UseUncachedPCIMappings",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type DWORD\nEncode -- Numeric Value\nCheck to see if we are converting PCI mappings"
    },
    {
      "name": "VarBusLinkWidth",
      "value_name": "VarBusLinkWidth",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "TEST ONLY FOR NOW\n0 - Do not vary PCI-E bus link width (default)\n1 - Vary PCI-E bus link width with performance\n2 - Vary PCI-E bug link width with performance but only allow increases in\nthe lane width (ie. never decrease the lane width).  See bug 320709\nfor more information.",
      "fields": [
        {
          "name": "VarBusLinkWidth",
          "bits": [0, 1],
          "states": [
            { "value": 0, "name": "DISABLE" },
            { "value": 1, "name": "ENABLE_BOTH" },
            { "value": 2, "name": "ENABLE_UPONLY" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "vbios",
      "value_name": "vbios",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type: Binary\nUsed to override the system memory copy of the VBIOS\nPut the entire 64K VBIOS in this registry key in binary format."
    },
    {
      "name": "vbios000",
      "value_name": "vbios000",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type: Binary\nWhen VBIOS size is over 65531 bytes, it just can't be correctly loaded by\none registry key by SetupApi SetupGetBinaryField() in INF. In the case,\nseparating vbios into registry keys, each size must be less than 65331 bytes\nVBIOS binary = vbios + [vbios000 + vbios001 + ...]\nBug 912315\n_INDEX:  Offset of index character\n_COUNT:  Count of vbios00x"
    },
    {
      "name": "VbiosFromROM",
      "value_name": "VbiosFromROM",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type: DWORD\nA non-zero value will cause the RM to ignore the vbios image from\ninstmem and read it directly from ROM\nTemp WAR for bug 169275"
    },
    {
      "name": "vbiosSource",
      "value_name": "vbiosSource",
      "key_paths": [
        "\\{4d36e968-e325-11ce-bfc1-08002be10318}\\"
      ],
      "bit_width": 32,
      "comment": "Type: Binary\nUsed as voltile registry entry only.  Saves the original VBIOS source."
    }
  ]
}
